      },
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}3(9^x)-6(6^x)+2(4^x)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nDivide by $4^x>0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}3\\left(\\frac94\\right)^x-6\\left(\\frac32\\right)^x+2&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nLet $u=(\\frac{3}{2})^x>0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}3u^2-6u+2&=0\\\\u&=\\frac{6\\pm\\sqrt{36-24}}{6}\\\\u&=1\\pm\\frac{\\sqrt3}{3}.\\end{align*}$$\nBoth values are positive, since $\\frac{\\sqrt3}{3}<1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\left(\\frac32\\right)^x&=1\\pm\\frac{\\sqrt3}{3}\\\\x&=\\log_{3/2}\\left(1\\pm\\frac{\\sqrt3}{3}\\right).\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
